# Build outputs.
_novo/

# The generated API page.  `novo doc` writes it here so a reader can
# see what the registry will serve, and the registry gets its own copy,
# uploaded beside the archive by `novo pkg publish`.  It is generated
# from the sources, so committing it would be committing a second
# original.
APIDOC.md

# The built package binary.  This package is a library and builds none.
# The line is here for when it grows a `main`.
/unicode-nv

# novo.lock is not ignored.  `docs/publishing.md` says to commit it,
# for a library as much as for an application.  It never ships, and it
# is what makes a build reproducible.  This package declares no
# dependencies, so the toolchain writes none, and the absence of the
# file is the empty lock.
